-- title:
--   Reducedness mod q of the finite-j chart ring
-- statement:
--   Fix a nonzero natural number $N_0$ and a prime $q$ with $q \nmid N_0$, and let $\mathbb{Z}_{(q)}$ denote the ring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt q`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8). Write $F$ for the full modular function field `modularFunctionFieldFull (N₀ * q)`, an intermediate field of the Laurent series field over $\mathbb{Q}$, and let $A =$ `IgusaScheme.chartAlgFin (N₀ * q) q` be the $\mathbb{Z}_{(q)}$-subalgebra of $F$ consisting of those elements that are integral over the $\mathbb{Z}_{(q)}$-subalgebra generated by the element `jFull (N₀ * q)` (the modular invariant $j$, given by its $q$-expansion); that is, $A$ is the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}_{(q)}[j]$ in $F$. Assume given a term $\mathfrak{P}$ of the structure `DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN`, which bundles the Igusa-scheme model `toBase N₀ q : X N₀ q ⟶ Spec ℤ_(q)` together with properness, flatness, local finite presentation, integrality of the total space, integral closedness of the sections over affine opens, a curve model over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ identified with the geometric generic fibre compatibly with the arithmetic Galois action and with $q$-expansions on the finite-$j$ chart, smoothness of relative dimension $1$ and geometric integrality of the generic fibre over $\mathbb{Q}$, cusp sections over the base, and further data summarised in that structure. The conclusion is that the quotient ring $A / qA$, where $qA$ is the ideal generated by the image of the natural number $q$, is reduced.
--
--   This records the reducedness of the special fibre at $q$ of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(N_0q)$ on the affine chart where $j$ is finite, in the bad-reduction case where $q$ divides the level $N_0q$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_finite_etale_quotient_span_aeval`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_finite_etale_quotient_span_aeval) in the analysis of the mod-$q$ fibre of the chart.
